{"nodes": [{"id": "plan_gmail", "label": "Gmail Ingest Plan", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "PLAN-GMAIL.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Phase 1b shipped. Records settled seams so the next lane is an edit. No LLM call on the poll path."}, {"id": "migrations_004_email_schema", "label": "004_email.sql", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PLAN-GMAIL.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "email_events ledger and applications table."}, {"id": "plan_gmail_g1_fixed_window", "label": "G1 Fixed Window Not historyId", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "PLAN-GMAIL.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Gmail has no history on a first run and drops it after about a week, so the catch-up query exists anyway. A stored cursor is a second path whose failure is a silently skipped window. newer_than:2d every tick, deduped by email_events, is one path. An outage longer than two days loses the gap."}, {"id": "plan_gmail_g2_two_dedupe_layers", "label": "G2 Two Dedupe Layers", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "PLAN-GMAIL.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "email_events (user_id, gmail_message_id) claims the message, including ignores and parse failures. expenses (user_id, source_ref) is the backstop, and a 23505 is success. applications has no unique source_ref because that column is overwritten with the email that last moved the row. The mailbox stays read-only; UNREAD is unused."}, {"id": "plan_gmail_g3_rules_not_model", "label": "G3 Rules Not a Model", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "PLAN-GMAIL.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Both original lanes are fixed templates. A Claude call per email, as evaluation section 9 imagined, spends money on text a regex reads exactly. Unparsed outcomes are the extension point: add a pattern, or later send only those messages to a model."}, {"id": "plan_gmail_g4_rejection_wins", "label": "G4 Any Rejection Phrase Wins", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "PLAN-GMAIL.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Receipt alone is applied. Receipt plus rejection, or rejection with no receipt, is rejected. The third shape is the common email and a receipt-versus-rejection framing misses it. Body and subject are both scanned."}, {"id": "plan_gmail_g5_praise_guard", "label": "G5 Praise Guard Is an Absence", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "PLAN-GMAIL.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Phrases like skills and background are impressive appear in rejections and in still-reviewing mail. REJECTION_PATTERNS matches the proceed/pursue/move-forward clause, and a test forbids praise phrases, instead of a combiner that undoes a bad entry."}, {"id": "plan_gmail_g6_company_key", "label": "G6 Key Applications on Company", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "PLAN-GMAIL.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Rejection mail often names a different role or none, so a (company, role) key would miss the row it exists to close. company_key drops punctuation and legal suffixes only. The index is not unique because applying twice to one company must stay possible."}, {"id": "plan_gmail_g7_orphan_rejection", "label": "G7 Orphan Rejection Becomes a Row", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "PLAN-GMAIL.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A rejection with no matching application is still inserted. A wrong row costs one correction; a dropped rejection is invisible. If no company can be extracted, the outcome is unparsed_application. Optimises recall, as evaluation section 9 asks."}, {"id": "plan_gmail_g8_sender_hint", "label": "G8 Sender Is a Hint", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "PLAN-GMAIL.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Gating Lane B on a noreply sender drops recruiter mail. Any receipt or rejection phrase routes to Lane B. The sender is still one rung of the company ladder, and ATS domains stop greenhouse.io being treated as the employer."}, {"id": "plan_gmail_g9_cards_match", "label": "G9 Match Cards Only via users.cards", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "PLAN-GMAIL.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No second allowlist. Longest match string wins so Chase does not steal Chase Freedom. No match leaves card null and still writes the row: a wrong card corrupts reconciliation, a null card is visibly incomplete."}, {"id": "plan_gmail_g10_spent_at_from_email", "label": "G10 spent_at From the Email", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "PLAN-GMAIL.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Use the date stated in the payment confirmation. If the email names none, use Gmail internalDate. now() would drift with when the poll happened to run."}, {"id": "plan_gmail_g11_raw_httpx", "label": "G11 Raw REST over httpx", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "PLAN-GMAIL.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A refresh-token grant and two GETs, about thirty lines, using httpx already in requirements. The Google client library would have added six packages. requirements.txt stays unchanged."}, {"id": "plan_gmail_g12_token_env_vars", "label": "G12 Tokens Are Per-mailbox Env Vars", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "PLAN-GMAIL.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "GMAIL_TOKEN_* is discovered by prefix. A JSON blob in one variable breaks because dotenv is sourced as a shell and braces expand. Stored ids are label:id because a Gmail message id is unique only inside one mailbox. Move to users.gmail_accounts when a second person uses this."}, {"id": "plan_gmail_lane_a", "label": "Lane A Card Bill Payments", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PLAN-GMAIL.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Payment-confirmation emails write an expenses row with kind cc_payment and status confirmed. Checked before the spend family so a settlement is never read as a swipe."}, {"id": "plan_gmail_lane_b", "label": "Lane B Job Applications", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PLAN-GMAIL.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Receipts and rejections upsert applications as applied or rejected. Not interview invites."}, {"id": "plan_gmail_lane_c", "label": "Lane C Swipe Alerts", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PLAN-GMAIL.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "You spent $X mail writes a pending spend. Amount, card, and date count immediately; meaning stays blank until the digest."}, {"id": "plan_gmail_email_events", "label": "email_events", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PLAN-GMAIL.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A row for every considered message, including ignore, parse failure, and error. Unique on (user_id, gmail_message_id). unparsed_* rows are the pattern backlog."}, {"id": "plan_gmail_applications", "label": "applications Table", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PLAN-GMAIL.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Keyed on company_key, not role. source_ref names the email that last moved the row and is not unique. An orphan rejection is still a row."}, {"id": "capabilities_gmail_poll", "label": "gmail poll", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "PLAN-GMAIL.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Hourly messages.list over newer_than:2d, then messages.get only for ids not already in email_events. One audit row per poll, path rules, model null."}, {"id": "capabilities_gmail_parse_route", "label": "route", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "PLAN-GMAIL.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Orders payment, then spend, then receipt or rejection, else ignore. The payment-before-spend order is the most important ordering in the file."}, {"id": "capabilities_gmail_accounts", "label": "gmail accounts", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "PLAN-GMAIL.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Scans the environment for GMAIL_TOKEN_* and polls each mailbox independently so one revoked token does not stop the others."}, {"id": "capabilities_gmail_write_payment", "label": "write_payment", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "PLAN-GMAIL.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Lane A write. Resolves the card being paid through users.cards match strings."}, {"id": "capabilities_gmail_upsert_application", "label": "upsert_application", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "PLAN-GMAIL.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Rejection updates the newest still-applied row for the company. A receipt matches the same role or an empty role. Otherwise insert."}, {"id": "core_db_seen_message_ids", "label": "seen_message_ids", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "PLAN-GMAIL.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One query for the hundred-odd ids in the window, not N existence checks. Steady state is a handful of messages.get calls an hour."}, {"id": "plan_gmail_privacy", "label": "Gmail Privacy Boundary", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PLAN-GMAIL.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Store the message id, sender, subject, and extracted scalars. Never store the body, snippet, HTML, OTPs, or full account numbers. The body is decoded, parsed, and dropped."}, {"id": "test_gmail_suite", "label": "test_gmail.py", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PLAN-GMAIL.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Offline email-rule checks, including praise that must not classify as a rejection and the double-write checks."}], "edges": [{"source": "plan_gmail", "target": "plan_v1", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "PLAN-GMAIL.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "plan_gmail", "target": "plan_expenses", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "PLAN-GMAIL.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "plan_gmail", "target": "evaluation_plan", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "PLAN-GMAIL.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "plan_gmail", "target": "requirements", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "PLAN-GMAIL.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "plan_gmail", "target": "plan_gmail_g1_fixed_window", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "PLAN-GMAIL.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "plan_gmail", "target": "plan_gmail_g2_two_dedupe_layers", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "PLAN-GMAIL.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "plan_gmail", "target": "plan_gmail_g3_rules_not_model", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "PLAN-GMAIL.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "plan_gmail", "target": "plan_gmail_g4_rejection_wins", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "PLAN-GMAIL.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "plan_gmail", "target": "plan_gmail_g5_praise_guard", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "PLAN-GMAIL.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "plan_gmail", "target": "plan_gmail_g6_company_key", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "PLAN-GMAIL.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "plan_gmail", "target": "plan_gmail_g7_orphan_rejection", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "PLAN-GMAIL.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "plan_gmail", "target": "plan_gmail_g8_sender_hint", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file